# Target C: two-wave odd-shell fold and a two-isolate obstruction

Date: 2026-10-08. Research start:
`c981b6f818764765bcb99917a9d858599c425471`.
Fixed main: `e0343614eac964a57273b564d0b1bd673f821f3e`.
State: `2026-10-08.audit.158` (through independent Audit.162).
Classification: **proved candidate awaiting independent audit**, with an
explicit **regression** against universal fold compatibility.
Registry status: unreviewed; canonical=false. C-II and Level I remain open.

The attempted chain was

`contact-preserving finite shell fold -> all actual upper constraints
strict -> full-source equal-cardinality strict diameter competitor`.

The first two implications hold for the regular shell. The last
requires the lower constraints involving every interior source point.
Two strict contact isolates can obstruct every cyclic version of the
fold. No universal source endpoint is obtained.

## 1. A finite endpoint with only two fixed adjacent vertices

Let q=2m+1 be odd, q>=21, alpha=pi/q, and
R=1/(2 sin alpha). Let v_j=R(exp(2ij alpha)) denote the vertices of the
regular unit q-gon, interpreted as planar vectors. Its diameter is
D=2R cos(alpha/2). Set

```
t=sin(alpha)^2=1/(4R^2), c=cos(2alpha)=1-2t,
a=2c-1=1-4t=1-1/R^2,
b=2ac-1=1-12t+16t^2=1-3/R^2+1/R^4.
```

First reflect each even-indexed vertex 0,2,...,2m-2 across the
line through its two original contact neighbors. These vertices are
pairwise nonadjacent; each reflected point is a v_j. Then reflect
the odd-indexed vertices 1,3,...,2m-3 across the lines through their
two already-reflected neighbors. These points become b v_j.
Leave v_{2m-1},v_{2m} fixed. Every stage is an explicitly defined
finite reflection. No claim is made that the intervening linear
paths are feasible.

The endpoint consists of factors a on the m even vertices, b on the
m-1 indicated odd vertices, and 1 on the two remaining vertices.
All original contacts remain exactly unit, since

```
a^2+1-2ac=4t,
a^2+b^2-2abc=4t,
2(1-c)=4t.
```

These are polynomial identities, not interval conclusions about equality.

For q>=21, alpha<1/6, t<1/36, and b>2/3; also a>b>0.
Any nonadjacent old pair has length at least 2 cos alpha>3/2.
For positive radial factors lambda_i,lambda_j>=b,

```
|lambda_i v_i-lambda_j v_j|^2
=R^2[(lambda_i-lambda_j)^2
     +2 lambda_i lambda_j(1-cos(theta_i-theta_j))]
>=b^2 |v_i-v_j|^2.
```

Thus every new nonadjacent pair is strictly longer than one.
The endpoint has exactly the original q-cycle of contacts and is
triangle-free.

Every pair except the fixed adjacent pair has at least one factor
at most a, and its length is at most

```
R(1+a)=2R cos(2alpha)<2R cos(alpha/2)=D.
```

The fixed pair has length one<D. Hence the endpoint strictly shortens
every actual diameter and has full diameter strictly below D.

This does not contradict the canonical shell stress or mixed
rigidity: it is a finite jump to another configuration, rather
than a feasible local path from the stressed shell.

## 2. The precise sufficient interior clearance

Let the full source consist of this wall and any unit-separated
cloud X strictly inside its convex hull. Suppose additionally that

```
|x-v_j|>1+3/R  for every x in X and every j.
```

Retain every cloud point at its original position during the fold.
The wall displacement is 1/R on the first wave and
3/R-1/R^3<3/R on the second, so all wall-cloud lower constraints remain
strictly above one. Cloud-cloud pairs retain their separation.

For upper constraints, every moving wall point has norm at most aR,
and every interior cloud point has norm strictly below R. Their
distances are at most R(1+a)<D. The fixed-wall/cloud and cloud/cloud
pairs retain their old strict upper slack: a strict interior point
of the wall polygon cannot be an endpoint of a diameter pair.
The endpoint is therefore a full-source equal-cardinality strict
diameter competitor.

The added clearance is a hypothesis. Canonical contact isolation
provides only distance strictly above one, with no bound of 3/R.
This result cannot be applied to arbitrary C-II sources.

## 3. Two contact isolates obstruct every rotated fold

For odd q>=65, R>10. Write delta=1/(100R^2), and put one paired
midpoint blocker on each of the two wall sides (0,1) and (2,3),
at radius

```
T=R cos(alpha)-sqrt((1+delta)^2-1/4).
```

Use the midpoint ray of each indicated side. This is the paired
placement from
[canonical Audit.65](../audits/target_c_odd_shell_barrier_payment_independent_audit_2026-10-06.md),
using only two of its collar points. Both blockers are strictly
inside the polygon. Each is at distance exactly 1+delta from
its two wall endpoints, and farther from all other wall points.
Both radii exceed R-2. Their angular separation is 4alpha, so
their mutual distance is

```
2T sin(2alpha)>2(1-2/R)cos(alpha)>1.
```

They are genuine contact isolates. Their radial depth h=R-T is
greater than sqrt(3)/2>4/5.

If a wall endpoint of either selected side moves inward radially
by d, its new squared distance from that side's blocker changes by

```
-2d(R-T cos(alpha))+d^2.
```

Each moved vertex in this fold has 1/R<=d<3/R. Therefore the
decrease in squared distance exceeds

```
d(8/5-3/R)>13/(10R).
```

The old excess above one is 2delta+delta^2<3/(100R^2), smaller than
this decrease. Every moved endpoint of a selected side collides
with its blocker.

Each cyclicly rotated fold fixes only two consecutive vertices.
It cannot fix all four endpoints of the two disjoint selected
sides. At least one endpoint of a selected side moves, so every
one of the q rotated folds has a certified collision.

These obstructions coexist with all strict diameter upper
constraints at every proposed endpoint. They concern the actual
full source and survive adding a deep cloud. Counting the number
of distinct folds does not produce an injective blocker payment:
the supports of these folds overlap over almost the entire shell.

This does not contradict Audit.65's (q+1)/2 payment for obstructing
q individual one-vertex proposals. The present motions move q-2
vertices each; two blockers can cover all of these large supports.

## 4. Quadratic deep fill and certified nonglobality

Add any unit-separated cloud inside the open disk of radius R-3.
Its separation from the wall exceeds three and from the blockers
exceeds one. This disk is strictly inside the wall polygon.
The old actual diameter pairs remain exactly the q wall-star
pairs, and the only contacts remain the wall cycle if the
deep cloud has internal distances strictly above one.

These are nonglobal configurations, even with quadratic cloud
population. This follows for any unit-separated deep cloud,
without assuming a specific lattice phase.

Let a_0=sqrt(3)/2. Oler's bound in the radius R-3 disk gives

```
z<=pi(R-3)^2/a_0+pi(R-3)+1.
```

Also q<2pi R. A comparison triangular lattice in a disk of radius
D/2 has limiting translation-average count

```
M=pi(D/2)^2/a_0
 =pi R^2/a_0-pi/[8a_0(1+cos(alpha))].
```

For n=q+2+z,

```
M-n>
(6pi/a_0-3pi)R-9pi/a_0+3pi-3
-pi/[8a_0(1+cos(alpha))]
>3pi R-(61/4)pi-3>0.
```

Here 1/2<a_0<1, cos alpha>0, R>10, and pi>3 suffice
for the conservative last bound. By continuity choose lattice
spacing strictly above one and disk radius strictly below D/2
while keeping translation-average count greater than n.
Translation averaging then supplies at least n sites; taking n
of them gives a whole-source strict diameter competitor.

Consequently neither two blockers nor a quadratic deep population
makes these sources global minimizers. The family is a compatibility
regression, not a Level I disproof.

## 5. Computation and disposition

[The checker](../../research/verify_target_c_two_wave_shell_fold_2026_10_08.py)
proves the four contact/reflection polynomial identities exactly.
Using the directed integer interval arithmetic of the canonical
Audit.65 verifier, it checks q=65,101,201: old and new shell
noncontact pairs; all new shell upper pairs; the exact old
diameter-star classification; strict old blocker-wall distances;
and blocker collisions for every cyclic cut.

It also constructs quadratic strict triangular-lattice clouds in
the radius R-3 disk and certifies their radial separation.
For spacing ell=1+q^-2, all indices with
|i|,|j|<=floor((R-3)/(2ell)) have squared lattice norm at most
3(R-3)^2/4, so these clouds have quadratic population.
All cloud pairs are certified by the positive integral lattice
norm, rather than by a subset of pair samples. The universal
finite-fold and obstruction claims use the analytic arguments
above; the finite cases are additional checks.

The source scope is a regular wall. No arbitrary canonical
wall, 3/R cloud clearance, compatible cloud rearrangement, or
global maximum-population classification has been extracted.
The C-II replacement step remains open.
